N5008 [over.best.ics.general]/4 only restricts the conversions for the
constructor candidates of one copy-initialization; a SFINAE probe nested in
that resolution (a constrained default template argument of a constructor
template, [temp.deduct.general]/5 + [temp.deduct]/8) is a separate overload
resolution and keeps the derived-to-base conversion
([over.best.ics.general]/6).  This is the libstdc++ 11 basic_string /
_RequireInputIter / is_convertible shape behind the Ubuntu 22.04 failures of
cpp11_conversion_function_template_copy_init and cpp11_locale_ctype_facet.
